# The browser in the desktop's Applications menu. A fragment, not a whole menu:
# the outer [begin]/[end] and the Applications submenu belong to kits/desktop,
# which parses every file in this directory in alphabetical order. Nothing
# breaks when the desktop kit is absent -- there is then no fluxbox to read it.
#
# 10, ahead of the burp kit's 20, because this is the entry someone opens
# casually and Burp is the one they open deliberately.
#
# NOT WRAPPED IN xterm, unlike the Burp entry, and the difference is real rather
# than stylistic: burp-start.sh's first run is a console conversation that
# blocks on stdin, whereas this never needs input. What a menu [exec] cannot do
# is report a failure -- fluxbox does not notice a failed exec, so a broken
# entry is silently inert -- which is why `browser` detaches, watches the
# process for three seconds, and raises an xmessage dialog when it finds no
# terminal to complain to.
[exec] (Web Browser) {/home/agent/bin/browser}
